    "Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play.",
    "Jins Hijaz is a 4-note jins. It is notated here with its tonic on D and its ghammaz on G. The interval between the 2nd and 3rd degrees is usually played smaller than notated by raising the 2nd a little and lowering the 3rd a little. Jins Hijaz is the first jins in Maqam Hijaz, Maqam Hijazkar, and Maqam Zanjaran."
  ],
  "text": "Jins Hijaz Root jins of the Maqam Hijaz Family Jins Index Pronunciation of Hijaz Click the notes and hold using the mouse to hear them play. Jins Hijaz is a 4-note jins . It is notated here with its tonic on D and its ghammaz on G. The interval between the 2 nd and 3 rd degrees is usually played smaller than notated by raising the 2 nd a little and lowering the 3 rd a little. Jins Hijaz is the first jins in Maqam Hijaz , Maqam Hijazkar , and Maqam Zanjaran . Ana Fi-ntizarak (1943) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt) Aghadan Alqak (1971) Umm Kulthum Music by Muhammad Abdel Wahab (Egypt) Bi Karm el-Lulu Fairouz Music by Philemon Wehbe el-Awwila Fil-Gharam(1944) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt) el-Ward Gamil (1946) Umm Kulthum Music by Zakariya Ahmad (Egypt)",
